{title: Splendor of Holiness}
{subtitle: Psalms 29:2}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [Dm] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]Heavenly beings lift your [Bb]voice
Give the glo[F]ry that he de[C]serves
Give the [Bb]strength [C]that he [Dm]has
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
The [Bb]name is great and ho[Dm]ly
[Bb]Bow down in his pre[C]sence
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
As[Dm]cribe to the Lord the glory
[Bb]Of his name in the [F]light [C]
[Dm]Worship the Lord in the splendor
[Bb]Of holiness to[F]night
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [C] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [Dm] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]His voice is over the [Bb]waters
[F]God of glory thun[C]ders
[Dm]Over the mighty deep [Bb]places
[F]Powerful and full of [C]majesty
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Pre-Chorus (repeat)}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
As[Dm]cribe to the Lord the glory
[Bb]Of his name in the [F]light [C]
[Dm]Worship the Lord in the splendor
[Bb]Of holiness to[F]night [C]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
He [Bb]shatters the [C]cedars
[Dm]The cedars of Lebanon
[Bb]The voice breaks [C]the forest
[Dm]The power is [Bb]upon us
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[C]Splendor of [Dm]holi[Bb]ness
Glory to the [F]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [F] | [C] | [Dm] | [Bb] |
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
